{"type":"message","id":"bba4264d","parentId":"1c89599d","timestamp":"2026-05-31T05:15:48.637Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The worker is returning 500 with \"error code: 1101\" - this is a Cloudflare Workers error meaning \"No domain\" or the worker can't be found. The worker might have an issue or the route isn't properly configured. GET requests work (which also hit the worker), but POST /send fails.\n\nActually wait - the GET requests returned valid data, but the POST returned 500. This could mean:\n1. The worker exists and handles GET but POST endpoint has an issue\n2. The /send path might not be correct\n3. The worker code has a bug in the POST handler\n\nLet me try different approaches - maybe the endpoint is different, like /api/send or the body needs different fields.","thinkingSignature":"035d7a7e8b268693cecc698463c057da7b2477f5ae0a3ea5e183348ed02c7bd8"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_cyg2o2ktadcx_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/\" -H \"X-API-KEY: ***\" | head -100"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_cyg2o2ktadcx_2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: ***\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"channel\":\"arbitration\",\"text\":\"[Heartbeat 05:15 UTC] Platform check.\"}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":304,"output":305,"cacheRead":21184,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":21793,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780204542551,"responseId":"066af6fff2dd07e69d5c810169eaec78"}}
